<p>
    <strong>Core Gameplan:</strong> Orzhov control variants leverage
    oppressive hand disruption (<a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Gerrard's Verdict">Gerrard's Verdict</a
    >, <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Duress"
        >Duress</a
    >) paired with versatile permanent destruction (<a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Vindicate">Vindicate</a
    >, <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Swords to Plowshares"
        >Swords to Plowshares</a
    >). In practice, this discard strategy actively plays into
    our strengths: discarding fatal enchantment clusters simply
    accelerates our graveyard setup for a terminal <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Replenish">Replenish</a
    > resolution.
</p>
<p>
    <strong>Sideboard Strategy:</strong> Anticipate heavy graveyard
    disruption (<a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Withered Wretch">Withered Wretch</a
    >, <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Tormod's Crypt">Tormod's Crypt</a
    >) and enchantment tax structures (<a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Aura of Silence">Aura of Silence</a
    >). Bring in <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Exalted Angel">Exalted Angel</a
    > as an unstoppable morph threat, alongside instant-speed answers
    like <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Disenchant">Disenchant</a
    > and <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Seal of Cleansing">Seal of Cleansing</a
    >. Avoid prolonged resource standoffs; force decisive
    exchanges while their removal targets are misaligned.
</p>
